COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment.parental_status IS 'Indicates whether segment targets parents, non-parents, or all. Nullable if parental status is not a qualification criterion.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment.purchase_history_flag IS 'Indicates whether segment qualification includes past purchase behavior from CRM or e-commerce data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment.refresh_cadence IS 'Frequency at which segment membership is recalculated and updated: real-time (streaming), hourly, daily, weekly, monthly, or static (one-time build).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment.rfm_score IS 'RFM segmentation score (e.g., 555 for best customers, 111 for low-value) used for behavioral qualification. Nullable if RFM is not a qualification criterion.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment.search_intent_keywords IS 'Comma-separated list of search keywords or intent signals used for behavioral qualification (e.g., ''luxury cars'', ''mortgage refinance''). Nullable if search intent is not a qualification criterion.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment.size IS 'Total count of unique users, devices, or households currently qualifying for this segment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment.vals_segment IS 'VALS psychographic segmentation classification (e.g., Innovators, Thinkers, Achievers, Experiencers) used for psychographic qualification. Nullable if VALS is not a qualification criterion. Code set: ref.vals_segment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE audience.taxonomy IS 'Reference taxonomy for standardized audience classification categories — aligned to IAB Audience Taxonomy v1.1 and custom agency extensions. Captures taxonomy node ID, parent node, category name, category level (tier 1/2/3), IAB standard code, description, applicable data types (behavioral/demographic/contextual), and active status. Provides the controlled vocabulary for consistent segment classification across campaigns, platforms, and reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.taxonomy_id IS 'Unique identifier for the audience taxonomy node. Primary key for the audience taxonomy reference structure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.parent_taxonomy_id IS 'Reference to the parent node in the taxonomy hierarchy. Null for top-level (tier 1) categories. Enables hierarchical navigation and roll-up reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.primary_replacement_taxonomy_id IS 'Reference to the taxonomy node that replaces this deprecated category. Null for active categories or deprecated categories without direct replacement. Enables automated migration of historical segments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.applicable_platforms IS 'Comma-separated list of digital platforms and channels where this taxonomy category is applicable (e.g., display, video, social, search, CTV, DOOH). Guides media planners on appropriate channel selection.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.average_cpm_usd IS 'Average cost per thousand impressions in US dollars for media buys targeting this audience category. Based on historical campaign data and current market rates. Used for budget planning and cost estimation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.category_description IS 'Detailed description of the audience category, including defining characteristics, typical behaviors, and use cases. Provides guidance for media planners and data analysts on appropriate segment application.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.category_name IS 'Human-readable name of the audience taxonomy category. Used in campaign planning interfaces, reporting dashboards, and client presentations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.cdp_integration_enabled IS 'Indicates whether this taxonomy category is integrated with Customer Data Platform for unified customer profile enrichment and personalization. True enables real-time audience orchestration across owned channels.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.comscore_compatible IS 'Indicates whether this taxonomy category can be mapped to Comscore digital audience measurement segments for cross-platform analytics and validation. True enables independent third-party audience verification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.consent_required IS 'Indicates whether explicit user consent is required under GDPR, CCPA, or other privacy regulations before using this audience category for targeting. True requires documented consent; false indicates legitimate interest or non-regulated data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.cpm_last_updated_date IS 'Date when the average CPM value was last refreshed from campaign performance data and market intelligence. Indicates pricing data freshness.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.data_source_type IS 'Classification of the data source origin for this audience category. First-party data is owned by the advertiser, second-party is partner-shared, third-party is purchased from data providers. Deterministic uses known identifiers; probabilistic uses inferred signals.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.data_type IS 'Primary data classification type for this audience category. Indicates the source and nature of the audience signal used for segmentation and targeting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.deprecation_reason IS 'Explanation for why this taxonomy category was deprecated or retired. Includes migration guidance to replacement categories. Null for active categories.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.dmp_integration_enabled IS 'Indicates whether this taxonomy category is integrated with the agency Data Management Platform for audience activation and cross-platform targeting. True enables automated segment sync to DSPs and SSPs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.dsp_activation_enabled IS 'Indicates whether this taxonomy category is available for programmatic activation via Demand-Side Platforms such as The Trade Desk. True enables real-time bidding and automated audience targeting in programmatic campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.effective_end_date IS 'Date when this taxonomy category was deprecated or retired. Null for currently active categories. Supports historical campaign analysis and taxonomy lifecycle management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.effective_start_date IS 'Date when this taxonomy category became available for use. Supports historical analysis and version control of taxonomy evolution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.estimated_reach IS 'Estimated total addressable audience size (unique users or devices) for this taxonomy category across all integrated platforms. Updated periodically based on DMP and CDP data. Used for media planning and feasibility assessment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.exclusion_categories IS 'Comma-separated list of taxonomy codes that should be excluded when this category is used, to prevent audience overlap or conflicting targeting logic. Enforces mutually exclusive segment rules.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.iab_standard_code IS 'Official IAB Audience Taxonomy standard code for this category. Null for custom agency extensions not covered by IAB standard. Enables industry-standard audience classification and cross-publisher comparison.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.is_active IS 'Indicates whether this taxonomy category is currently active and available for use in campaign planning and targeting. False indicates deprecated or sunset categories that should not be used in new campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.last_reviewed_date IS 'Date when this taxonomy category was last reviewed for accuracy, relevance, and compliance. Supports taxonomy governance and quality assurance processes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.minimum_segment_size IS 'Minimum number of unique users or devices required for this audience category to be activated in campaigns. Enforces privacy thresholds and prevents re-identification risk. Typically set to 1000+ for GDPR compliance and platform minimums.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.nielsen_compatible IS 'Indicates whether this taxonomy category can be mapped to Nielsen audience measurement segments for GRP and TRP calculation. True enables cross-platform reach and frequency planning using Nielsen Ad Intel data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.path IS 'Full hierarchical path from root to this node, using forward-slash delimiter (e.g., Demographics/Age/18-24). Enables breadcrumb navigation and full-path filtering in reporting tools.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.privacy_classification IS 'Privacy sensitivity level of the audience data in this category. Non-PII contains no personal identifiers, pseudonymous uses hashed or tokenized IDs, PII-based includes direct identifiers, sensitive includes special category data under GDPR Article 9.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.reach_last_updated_date IS 'Date when the estimated reach value was last refreshed from source systems. Indicates data freshness for media planning decisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.taxonomy_code IS 'Unique alphanumeric code identifying this taxonomy node. Used for system integration and cross-platform mapping. Follows agency naming convention.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.taxonomy_level IS 'Hierarchical tier level of this taxonomy node. Tier 1 represents top-level categories, tier 2 represents sub-categories, tier 3 represents granular segments. Supports drill-down analysis and hierarchical reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.usage_guidelines IS 'Best practice guidance and restrictions for using this audience category in campaigns. Includes recommended use cases, exclusion scenarios, and compliance considerations. Supports media planners and account teams in appropriate segment application.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.version_number IS 'Version identifier for this taxonomy node, following semantic versioning convention (major.minor.patch). Tracks taxonomy evolution and enables version-specific reporting and analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.taxonomy.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE audience.activation IS 'Operational record of an audience segment being activated (pushed) to a specific DSP, SSP, or media platform for campaign targeting. Captures activation date, target platform (The Trade Desk, DV360, Meta, etc.), segment ID, activation status (pending/active/expired/paused), estimated reach, match rate, activation method (pixel, API, S2S), and associated campaign reference. Tracks the operational lifecycle of audience deployment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.activation_id IS 'Unique identifier for the audience activation record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.activation_platform_audience_audience_segment_id IS 'External identifier assigned by the target platform (DSP/SSP) for this activated audience segment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.activation_segment_id IS 'Reference to the audience segment being activated for targeting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.asset_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.asset. Business justification: Activations push segments to DSPs/SSPs with specific creative; programmatic campaigns require asset-segment pairing for trafficking, and activation records must track which creative serves to each aud LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.budget_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.budget_line. Business justification: Each audience activation to a DSP/platform consumes a specific budget line (media spend allocation). Finance teams reconcile activation costs against budget lines. This link enables activation-level s LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.budget_line.budget_line_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the campaign for which this audience segment is being activated. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: Activations are executed under a contract insertion order that authorizes spend, flight dates, and placement specs. Linking activation to contract_insertion_order enables contractual compliance tracki LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Activations carry cost_cpm and currency_code indicating direct media/data costs. Cost center attribution for audience activation spend is required for internal cost allocation, P&L reporting, and char LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.creative_deliverable_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.creative_deliverable. Business justification: Activations reference deliverables for media plan execution; trafficking workflows map segments to specific creative deliverables to ensure correct creative versions serve to each audience across chan LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.creative_deliverable.creative_deliverable_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: Audience activations are executed within specific campaign flights. Linking activation to flight enables flight-level audience delivery reporting, frequency management, and reach measurement within sc LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.flight.flight_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Audience activations are often executed as part of broader project initiatives for budget tracking, timeline management, and deliverable coordination. Agencies track which project initiative funded an LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.line_item_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.line_item. Business justification: Programmatic audience activations are executed at the line-item level. Buyers need to reconcile which audience activations drove delivery against specific line items for billing verification, performa LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.line_item.line_item_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.lookalike_model_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.lookalike_model. Business justification: When an audience activation pushes a lookalike-generated segment to a DSP or SSP, the activation record should reference the lookalike_model that produced the expanded audience. This enables performan';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Activations are executed through platform vendors (DSPs, social platforms, DMPs). Tracking which supplier/platform executed each activation is fundamental to reconciliation, performance reporting, inv LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.suppression_list_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.suppression_list. Business justification: audience_activation pushes segments to DSPs/SSPs. suppression_list defines identifiers to exclude from targeting. An activation should reference which suppression list was applied to ensure excluded i';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.tech_partner_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.tech_partner. Business justification: Audience activations are executed through DSP/tech platforms. Knowing which tech partner executed each activation is required for platform fee reconciliation, troubleshooting sync errors (retry_count, LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.tech_partner.tech_partner_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.activation_date IS 'Date when the audience segment was activated and pushed to the target platform.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.activation_method IS 'Technical method used to push the audience segment to the target platform. API = Application Programming Interface, S2S = Server-to-Server integration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.activation_name IS 'Business-friendly name or label for this activation instance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.activation_status IS 'Current operational status of the audience activation in its lifecycle.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.activation_timestamp IS 'Precise timestamp when the activation was initiated and the segment push began.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.activation_type IS 'Classification of the activation purpose and targeting strategy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.bid_modifier IS 'Multiplier applied to base bid amounts for this audience segment (e.g., 1.25 = 25% bid increase, 0.80 = 20% bid decrease).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.consent_framework IS 'Privacy consent framework applied to this activation. IAB TCF = Interactive Advertising Bureau Transparency and Consent Framework.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.consent_status IS 'Privacy consent status for the audience segment members at the time of activation, ensuring GDPR and CCPA compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.cost_cpm IS 'Cost per thousand impressions charged by the data provider or platform for activating this audience segment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for activation costs (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.data_source_type IS 'Origin classification of the audience data being activated (first-party = owned, second-party = partner, third-party = purchased).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.effective_end_date IS 'Date when the activated audience segment expires and is no longer available for targeting. Nullable for open-ended activations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.effective_start_date IS 'Date when the activated audience segment becomes available for targeting in campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.error_message IS 'Detailed error or failure message if the activation encountered issues during processing or sync.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.estimated_reach IS 'Estimated number of unique users or devices in the activated audience segment available for targeting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.frequency_cap IS 'Maximum number of times an individual user in the activated segment should be exposed to campaign creative within the frequency window.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.frequency_cap_window_hours IS 'Time window in hours over which the frequency cap is applied.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.last_sync_timestamp IS 'Timestamp of the most recent successful synchronization of audience data to the target platform.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.match_rate_percentage IS 'Percentage of audience segment records successfully matched and recognized by the target platform, expressed as a decimal (e.g., 75.50 for 75.5%).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.matched_user_count IS 'Actual number of users or devices successfully matched by the target platform during activation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.next_sync_timestamp IS 'Scheduled timestamp for the next audience data synchronization to the target platform.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.notes IS 'Free-form notes or comments about this activation for operational context and troubleshooting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.priority_level IS 'Business priority assigned to this activation for resource allocation and optimization decisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.retry_count IS 'Number of retry attempts made for failed activations before marking as permanently failed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.sync_frequency IS 'Cadence at which the audience segment membership is refreshed and re-synced to the target platform.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.unmatched_user_count IS 'Number of users or devices from the segment that could not be matched by the target platform.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.activation.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE audience.lookalike_model IS 'Operational record of a lookalike audience model built from a seed segment — capturing seed segment reference, model algorithm type (cosine similarity, gradient boosting, neural net), expansion ratio, similarity threshold, model training date, model version, platform (The Trade Desk, DV360), estimated reach, validation accuracy, and model status. Enables scale expansion of high-value audience segments for prospecting campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.lookalike_model_id IS 'Unique identifier for the lookalike audience model record. Primary key for the lookalike model entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the advertiser or client account that owns this lookalike model for campaign use and billing purposes. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Lookalike models are built for specific brands to expand reach among new audiences resembling existing brand customers. Brand managers need to track which lookalike models are active for their brand f LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.campaign_id IS 'Optional reference to a specific campaign for which this lookalike model was created, enabling campaign-specific audience modeling strategies. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: Lookalike models are commissioned and billed under specific contract IOs in programmatic advertising. Linking to contract_insertion_order enables cost attribution, IO-level model performance reporting LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Lookalike models carry model_cost and currency_code attributes. Cost center attribution for model development and licensing costs is required for internal P&L reporting and chargeback in agencies that LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.development_initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Lookalike model development is a distinct project deliverable with dedicated timelines, resources, and budgets. Agencies track which initiative funded model creation for cost recovery and to manage da LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.segment_id IS 'Reference to the source audience segment used as the foundation for building the lookalike model. The seed segment contains high-value users whose characteristics are modeled.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Lookalike models are frequently built by third-party data science platforms or DSPs (e.g., Facebook, Trade Desk, LiveRamp). Tracking the supplier is essential for cost allocation, model performance at LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.taxonomy_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.taxonomy. Business justification: A lookalike model is built to expand a seed audience into a broader audience within a specific audience category. The taxonomy_id FK classifies the lookalike model under the standardized IAB Audience';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.tech_partner_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.tech_partner. Business justification: Lookalike models are built and hosted on specific DSP/ML tech platforms. platform_name is a plain-text denormalization of the tech partner. FK enables model governance, platform fee tracking, and plat LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.tech_partner.tech_partner_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.algorithm_type IS 'Machine learning algorithm used to build the lookalike model. Determines the mathematical approach for identifying similar audience members. Code set: ref.algorithm_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.baseline_performance_value IS 'Benchmark performance metric value from the seed segment, used to compare lookalike audience performance against the original high-value segment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.consent_compliant_flag IS 'Indicates whether the lookalike model was built using only users who provided explicit consent for data usage under GDPR, CCPA, or other privacy regulations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for the model cost and related financial metrics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.data_source_type IS 'Classification of the data used to build the seed segment and train the model. First-party is owned data; second-party is partner data; third-party is purchased data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.estimated_reach IS 'Projected number of unique users or devices in the lookalike audience available for targeting across campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.expansion_ratio IS 'Multiplier indicating how many times larger the lookalike audience is compared to the seed segment (e.g., 10.00 means the lookalike is 10x the seed size). Used to balance reach vs. similarity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.expiration_date IS 'Date when the lookalike model is scheduled to expire and become unavailable for targeting unless refreshed or extended.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.feature_set IS 'Comma-separated list of data attributes used as input features for model training (e.g., demographics, behavioral signals, purchase history, engagement metrics).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.geographic_scope IS 'Geographic boundary for the lookalike audience (e.g., USA, CAN, GBR, global). Uses ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country codes or ''global'' for worldwide reach.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.last_refresh_date IS 'Date when the lookalike model was most recently retrained or refreshed with updated seed segment data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.model_cost IS 'Total cost incurred to build and deploy the lookalike model, including data acquisition, platform fees, and computational resources.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.model_description IS 'Detailed business description of the lookalike model purpose, target use cases, and strategic rationale for campaign planners and media buyers.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.model_name IS 'Business-friendly name assigned to the lookalike model for identification and campaign planning purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.model_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the lookalike model. Active models are available for campaign targeting; expired models require retraining.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.model_version IS 'Version identifier for the lookalike model, enabling tracking of model iterations and A/B testing across versions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.next_refresh_date IS 'Scheduled date for the next model retraining cycle based on the refresh frequency policy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.performance_metric_type IS 'Primary Key Performance Indicator (KPI) used to evaluate the lookalike model effectiveness in campaigns. CTR = Click-Through Rate, CVR = Conversion Rate, ROAS = Return on Ad Spend, CPA = Cost Per Acquisition, LTV = Lifetime Value.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.refresh_frequency_days IS 'Number of days between scheduled model retraining cycles to maintain accuracy and relevance as audience behaviors evolve.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.similarity_threshold IS 'Minimum similarity score (0.0000 to 1.0000) required for a user to be included in the lookalike audience. Higher thresholds produce smaller, more similar audiences.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.training_date IS 'Date when the lookalike model was trained on the seed segment data. Critical for understanding model freshness and performance decay over time.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.validation_accuracy IS 'Model accuracy score (0.0000 to 1.0000) measured on a holdout validation dataset, indicating how well the model predicts high-value user characteristics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.lookalike_model.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE audience.segment_membership IS 'Association record linking individual audience identifiers (cookie IDs, device IDs, hashed emails, MAIDs) to specific audience segments. Captures membership start date, expiry date, membership source, confidence score, inclusion/exclusion flag, and last refresh timestamp. Enables real-time segment population tracking and audience size reporting across DMP, CDP, and DSP platforms including The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.segment_membership_id IS 'Unique identifier for the segment membership record. Primary key for the segment membership association.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.budget_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.budget_line. Business justification: Segment membership has cost_per_member indicating data costs that must be tracked against a budget line. Audience data spend management requires linking membership costs to approved budget lines for v LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.budget_line.budget_line_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Segment membership records carry cost_per_member and currency_code, indicating per-member data costs. Cost center attribution is required for internal billing and data cost allocation reporting across LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Segment membership records are generated during initiative execution (e.g., audience onboarding initiative, data partnership initiative). Linking membership to the originating initiative enables attri LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.segment_id IS 'Reference to the specific audience segment that this identifier belongs to. Links to the audience segment definition in the DMP or CDP.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Segment membership data is sourced from third-party data suppliers. Media planners need supplier attribution per membership record for data cost reconciliation, quality audits, and GDPR data processor LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.tech_partner_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.tech_partner. Business justification: Segment memberships are activated via DSP/tech platforms. dsp_platform is a plain-text denormalization of the tech partner. Linking to tech_partner enables platform fee reconciliation, activation trou LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.tech_partner.tech_partner_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.activation_status IS 'The status of this segment membership in the DSP or activation platform. Activated indicates the membership is live and available for targeting. Pending indicates activation is in progress. Failed indicates activation encountered an error. Deactivated indicates the membership has been removed from the activation platform.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.activation_timestamp IS 'The timestamp when this segment membership was successfully activated in the DSP or targeting platform. Used for activation latency analysis and real-time audience availability reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.audience_identifier IS 'The individual audience identifier (cookie ID, device ID, hashed email, MAID, or other pseudonymous identifier) that is a member of the segment. This is the core identifier used for targeting and activation across DSP, DMP, and CDP platforms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.confidence_score IS 'A numeric score between 0 and 1 representing the confidence or probability that the audience identifier truly belongs to this segment. Higher scores indicate stronger membership signals. Used for quality filtering and bid optimization in programmatic campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.cost_per_member IS 'The cost paid to acquire or license this specific segment membership from a third-party data provider, expressed in the campaign currency. Null for first-party segments. Used for data cost attribution and ROI analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.currency_code IS 'The three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the cost per member amount (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP). Used for multi-currency data cost reporting and financial reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.device_type IS 'The type of device associated with this audience identifier. Desktop indicates traditional computer. Mobile indicates smartphone. Tablet indicates tablet device. CTV indicates Connected TV. OTT indicates Over-The-Top streaming device. Other indicates unclassified device. Used for device-specific targeting and cross-device attribution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.frequency_cap IS 'The maximum number of times this audience identifier should be exposed to ads from campaigns targeting this segment within a defined time period. Used for frequency management and preventing ad fatigue. Nullable if no cap is applied.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.geographic_region IS 'The geographic region or market associated with this segment membership, if the segment has geographic targeting criteria. Used for geo-targeted campaign planning and regional audience analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.identifier_type IS 'The type of audience identifier used for this membership record. Indicates whether the identifier is a cookie ID, mobile advertising ID (MAID), device ID, hashed email, customer ID, or household ID.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.inclusion_flag IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether this is an inclusion (true) or exclusion (false) membership. Inclusion memberships are targeted in campaigns; exclusion memberships are suppressed. Supports negative targeting and suppression list management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.last_refresh_timestamp IS 'The timestamp when this segment membership record was last refreshed or re-evaluated. Critical for real-time segment population tracking and ensuring audience data freshness for DSP activation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.match_rate IS 'The rate at which this audience identifier successfully matched to the segment criteria, expressed as a decimal between 0 and 1. Used for data quality assessment and segment match performance analysis across DMP and CDP integrations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.membership_expiry_date IS 'The date when the segment membership expires or is scheduled to expire. Nullable for evergreen segments. Used for time-bound segment management and automated exclusion workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.membership_source IS 'The origin or derivation method of the segment membership. First-party indicates data collected directly by the advertiser. Second-party indicates data shared by a partner. Third-party indicates data purchased from a data provider. Modeled indicates membership derived from predictive modeling. Lookalike indicates membership based on similarity to a seed audience. Behavioral indicates membership based on observed actions. Contextual indicates membership based on content consumption. Code set: ref.membership_source.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.membership_start_date IS 'The date when the audience identifier first became a member of this segment. Used for recency analysis and segment freshness reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.membership_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the segment membership. Active indicates the identifier is currently in the segment and eligible for targeting. Expired indicates membership has lapsed. Excluded indicates the identifier has been explicitly removed. Pending indicates membership is being processed. Suppressed indicates the identifier is blocked from targeting due to consent or compliance rules.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.recency_days IS 'The number of days since the audience identifier last exhibited the behavior or attribute that qualifies them for this segment. Used for recency-based targeting strategies and segment decay analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.segment_priority IS 'A numeric priority ranking for this segment membership when the audience identifier belongs to multiple overlapping segments. Higher values indicate higher priority. Used for bid decisioning and creative selection when multiple segments apply.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.segment_membership.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE audience.suppression_list IS 'Audience suppression list record defining identifiers to be excluded from campaign targeting — including converted customers, opted-out users, competitor employees, brand safety exclusions, and frequency-capped audiences. Captures list name, suppression type, identifier type (hashed email, cookie, MAID), list size, source system, creation date, expiry date, and associated campaign or advertiser scope. Critical for privacy compliance and media efficiency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.suppression_list_id IS 'Unique identifier for the suppression list record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.advertiser_id IS 'Identifier of the advertiser to which this suppression list is scoped. Nullable if the list is shared across multiple advertisers. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Suppression lists are brand-specific in multi-brand advertisers — Brand A''s opted-out customers must not suppress Brand B campaigns. Brand-level suppression management is a standard privacy compliance LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.campaign_id IS 'Identifier of the specific campaign to which this suppression list is applied. Nullable if the list is applied at advertiser or account level. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: Suppression lists are applied at the IO level in media buying — the IO specifies which suppression lists govern a given buy to prevent serving ads to opted-out or excluded audiences. This link enables LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.creation_initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Suppression list creation and maintenance is often a project task within compliance or campaign setup initiatives. Agencies track which project funded list development for billing and to manage data o LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.data_supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: data_provider on suppression_list is a plain-text denormalization of the vendor supplier. Suppression list data is sourced from specific vendors (opt-out providers, CRM data vendors). FK enables vendo LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.enforcement_tech_partner_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.tech_partner. Business justification: Suppression lists are synced to and enforced by specific DSP/tech platforms. platform_integration_status and platform_sync_timestamp on suppression_list confirm a platform relationship exists. Complia LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.tech_partner.tech_partner_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: Suppression lists are applied at the flight level to exclude opted-out users or existing customers from specific flight executions. Media planners need flight-level suppression control for granular au LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.flight.flight_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.governing_agreement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.agreement. Business justification: Suppression obligations are frequently contractually mandated (competitor exclusions, brand safety requirements, regulatory compliance). Critical for compliance verification, audit trails, and ensurin LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.agreement.agreement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Suppression lists are often derived from segments (e.g., ''suppress all users who converted'' or ''suppress all users in segment X''). Adding source_segment_id tracks which segment the suppression list wa';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.approval_status IS 'Approval workflow status for the suppression list (approved, pending, rejected). Lists must be approved before activation in campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.approval_timestamp IS 'Timestamp when the suppression list was approved for use in campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.archive_date IS 'Date when the suppression list was archived and removed from active campaign targeting systems.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.consent_withdrawal_flag IS 'Indicates whether the suppression list contains identifiers for users who have withdrawn marketing consent (True/False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.data_cost IS 'Cost incurred to acquire or license the suppression list data from a third-party provider, in US Dollars (USD).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.effective_end_date IS 'Date when the suppression list expires and is no longer applied to campaign targeting. Nullable for indefinite suppression lists.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.effective_start_date IS 'Date from which the suppression list becomes active and is applied to campaign targeting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.frequency_cap_period IS 'Time period over which the frequency cap threshold is measured (hour, day, week, month, campaign lifetime).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.frequency_cap_threshold IS 'Maximum number of impressions or interactions allowed before an identifier is added to the suppression list. Applicable for frequency-capped suppression types.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.hashing_algorithm IS 'Cryptographic hashing algorithm applied to identifiers for privacy protection (SHA256, MD5, SHA1, none if identifiers are not hashed).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.identifier_type IS 'Type of identifier stored in the suppression list (hashed email, cookie ID, Mobile Advertising ID (MAID), device ID, customer ID, IP address). Determines matching strategy in Demand-Side Platforms (DSPs) and Supply-Side Platforms (SSPs).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.last_refresh_timestamp IS 'Timestamp of the most recent data refresh or sync operation for this suppression list.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.list_code IS 'Unique business code or external identifier for the suppression list used in campaign systems and Data Management Platforms (DMPs).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.list_name IS 'Business-friendly name of the suppression list (e.g., ''Q4 Converted Customers'', ''GDPR Opt-Out Master'', ''Competitor Employees'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.list_size IS 'Total count of unique identifiers in the suppression list. Used for reach estimation and media planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.list_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the suppression list (active, inactive, expired, pending approval, archived). Only active lists are applied to campaign targeting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.match_rate_percentage IS 'Percentage of identifiers in the suppression list that successfully matched against campaign targeting pools in Demand-Side Platforms (DSPs) or Data Management Platforms (DMPs). Used to assess list quality and reach impact.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.notes IS 'Free-form notes or comments about the suppression list for internal reference, including special handling instructions or business context.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.platform_integration_status IS 'Status of the suppression list synchronization with downstream advertising platforms such as Demand-Side Platforms (DSPs), Supply-Side Platforms (SSPs), or ad servers (synced, pending sync, sync failed, not applicable).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.platform_sync_timestamp IS 'Timestamp of the most recent successful synchronization of the suppression list to downstream advertising platforms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.privacy_compliance_flag IS 'Indicates whether the suppression list was created to satisfy privacy regulations such as General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) or California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) opt-out requests (True/False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.refresh_frequency IS 'Cadence at which the suppression list is refreshed or re-synced from the source system (daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, on-demand, real-time).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.retention_period_days IS 'Number of days the suppression list and its identifiers are retained before automatic archival or deletion, per data retention policies and privacy regulations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.scope_level IS 'Organizational level at which the suppression list is applied (global across all advertisers, advertiser-specific, campaign-specific, line-item-specific).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.source_file_name IS 'Name of the file or data feed from which the suppression list was ingested, if applicable. Supports audit and lineage tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.source_system IS 'Originating system or platform that generated the suppression list (e.g., ''Salesforce CRM'', ''The Trade Desk'', ''Adobe Audience Manager'', ''Google Campaign Manager 360'', ''Internal CRM'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.suppression_list_description IS 'Detailed business description of the suppression list purpose, use case, and any special handling instructions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.suppression_type IS 'Category of suppression defining why identifiers are excluded from targeting (converted customer, opted-out user, frequency-capped audience, competitor employee, brand safety exclusion, fraud prevention).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.creation_date IS 'Date when the suppression list was first created in the system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN audience.suppression_list.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';
